      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "At Para 40, the Hon'ble High Court of Delhi has observed as under:\n\"To summarise, a conspectus of the above-mentioned judicial precedents reveal the following :\n(i). Power under Section 156(3) Cr. PC necessitates application of judicial min"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9a0682fd9877437b9ca83e4469f34d98_91",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "( ii) Such power is to be exercised in a judicious manner, and cannot be exercised mechanically or arbitrarily."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8455ee6940fc464084399a5e33508477_92",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nLOVLEEN (iii) Magistrates cannot direct registration of FIR on Digitally signed Crl. Revision No:386/2024 Sub-Inspector Vikas Solanki vs. State page no. 11 of 14 by LOVLEEN Date: 2024.12.04 14:34:36 +0530 mere asking of complainant.\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3520df65f3804b848069d0b4fb85ae67_93",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
